{
  "schema_version": 1,
  "scenario_id": "hypothetical-same-year-contingent-recovery-v1",
  "currency": "GBP_nominal",
  "feedback_basis": "same_year_total_recovery_entitlement",
  "accounting": {
    "book_expense": "same_reporting_year",
    "cash_payment": "same_reporting_year",
    "tax_deduction": "same_reporting_year",
    "base_lease_pv_rou_liability": "excluded",
    "variable_allowance_posting": "separate_penny_posting_of_fraction_times_total_variable_rent"
  },
  "iteration_policy": {
    "domain": "finite_contractual_total_rent_grid",
    "max_steps": 128,
    "acceptance": "identical_fixed_point_from_zero_and_sum_of_caps"
  },
  "public_rules": [
    "FY2024 means 1 April 2023 through 31 March 2024. Each row explicitly states that reporting year's contingent-rent terms for all four leases. There is no inference from another year and no forecast amount is provided.",
    "For each payable lease, annual variable rent equals its stated rate times MAX(0, the same-year total recovery entitlement minus that lease's annual threshold), rounded half up to its stated GBP100 or GBP1000 contractual unit, then limited by its annual cap. Caps are whole contractual rounding units. The payable annual fee is not prorated for a partial fixed-rent reporting year. Inactive rows explicitly have zero rate and cap.",
    "Contingent rent is separately expensed, paid in cash and deducted for tax in the same reporting year. It is excluded from fixed-lease present value, right-of-use assets and lease liabilities. The existing fixed-rent lease terms and balances retain their original treatment.",
    "The separately stated variable eligibility fraction is applied to the TOTAL posted annual variable rent and rounded half up once to GBP0.01. This allowance is posted separately from the fixed-lease allowance. Do not combine the two amounts before rounding.",
    "Let v be total posted variable rent, A its separately posted eligible allowance, E0 the non-variable recovery basis including fixed-lease allowance but excluding current gross-up tax, and B0 the pre-variable gross-up taxable base. Current tax uses the existing regulatory loss policy at B0+A-v. Total recovery entitlement equals E0+A+current gross-up tax. Thus current entitlement and current variable rents determine one another.",
    "For positive taxable base B, continuous loss use is MIN(available old losses, loss-use-cap times B divided by (1-tax-rate times (1-loss-use-cap))). Separately post tax-rate times (B-continuous loss use)/(1-tax-rate) and continuous loss use to GBP0.01, half up. For B<=0 current tax and old-loss use are zero and the new loss is -B posted to pennies.",
    "Use the finite contractual fee grid. Accept a year only when monotonicity including penny postings is proved and iteration from both zero total rent and the sum of annual caps reaches the SAME fixed point within 128 steps. Different endpoint fixed points, an unproved monotonicity bound or failure to coalesce rejects the year. A continuous contraction heuristic is not a uniqueness certificate."
  ],
